**Calculation:**

 sqrt{(1-sin 3theta)/(1+sin 3theta)} 

⇒ By putting θ = 15° 

 sqrt{(1-sin 3theta)/(1+sin 3theta)} 

⇒ sqrt{(1-sin 45)/(1+sin 45)} 

⇒ sqrt{(1- (1/sqrt2))/(1+ (1/sqrt2))} = sqrt{(sqrt2 - 1)/(sqrt2 + 1)} 

⇒ sqrt{(sqrt2 - 1)/(sqrt2 + 1) times(sqrt2 - 1)/(sqrt2 - 1)} 

⇒ sqrt{((sqrt2 - 1)²)/(2-1)} 

⇒ sqrt{(sqrt2 - 1)²}

⇒ √2 - 1

Again, In option 1 By putting θ = 15° we get,

sec 3θ - tan 3θ = sec 45° - tan 45°

⇒ √2 - 1

**∴ The correct option is 1**

** [IMAGE: https://cdn.repeatermock.com/tb/c76c13ba2d2ab46b47f8a931ae621dac081a0cb266b142dc23f58659fac4a466.png] __Alternate Method__**

 sqrt{(1-sin 3theta)/(1+sin 3theta)} 

⇒ sqrt{{(1-sin 3theta)/(1+sin 3theta)} times(1-sin3theta)/(1-sin3theta)} 

⇒ sqrt{((1-sin 3theta)²)/(1²-sin² 3theta)} 

⇒ sqrt{((1-sin 3theta)²)/(cos² 3theta)} 

⇒ sqrt{((1-sin 3theta)/(cos 3theta)})² 

⇒ (1 - sin3theta)/(cos3theta)

⇒ (1)/(cos3theta)-(sin3theta)/(cos3theta)

⇒ sec 3θ - tan 3θ

∴ The correct option is 1
